.TH MONGOOSE 1 "September 2026" "mongoose 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mongoose \- copy one NFS path to another, then keep it in sync until cutover
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B copy
.BI \-\-src " URL"
.BI \-\-dst " URL"
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-exclude
.IR GLOB ]...
.RB [ \-\-parallel
.IR N ]
.br
.B mongoose
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.B sync
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-cutover ]
.RB [ \-\-parallel
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mongoose
copies everything under one NFS path to another NFS path from a single
host, speaking NFSv3 directly: nothing is mounted and nothing else is
installed. It scans the source with an embedded parallel walker, builds
a local index, and copies over raw NFSv3 with libnfs. After the initial
copy it can sync incrementally while the source stays live, finishing
with a verified cutover. Everything it needs to remember lives under one
work directory.
.PP
Run as root: libnfs binds reserved ports for AUTH_SYS. NFSv3 only.
Re-running a command with the same
.B \-\-work\-dir
resumes it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B copy
Full copy of
.B \-\-src
to
.BR \-\-dst .
Scans the source, builds the index under
.BR \-\-work\-dir ,
then copies. Safe to re-run: a completed scan is not repeated and
completed shards are skipped.
.TP
.B sync
Copy what changed on the source since the last copy or sync: rescan,
classify against the previous pass, copy only the difference. Repeat
while the source is live; finish with
.B \-\-cutover
once source writers are stopped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-src " URL"
Where to copy from:
.IR nfs://server/export[/path] .
.TP
.BI \-\-dst " URL"
Where to copy to:
.IR nfs://server/export[/path] .
Refused if it is the same path as the source, inside it, or a parent
of it on the same server.
.TP
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
Local directory for this job's index, checkpoints, and results. One job
per directory; reuse it to resume and to sync.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " GLOB"
Directory name pattern to skip, e.g.\&
.IR .snapshot .
Repeatable;
.B copy
only. Remembered in the work dir, so later syncs skip the same
directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-parallel " N"
How much to do at once: NFS connections, with scan workers and in-flight
files scaled to match. Default 32, maximum 100. Lower it if the source
or destination server is struggling; raise it if both are idle and the
copy is slow. Not sticky: stop, re-run with a different value, and the
job resumes at the new level.
.TP
.B \-\-cutover
.RB ( sync )
Final pass: source writers must be stopped. Copies nothing; fails if
anything still differs, so a clean exit means the trees have converged.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More logging.
.B \-v
shows engine detail,
.B \-vv
debug.
.BR RUST_LOG ,
when set, overrides this flag.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a deliberate SIGINT/SIGTERM stop (re-run the same
command to resume).
.TP
.B 1
Error (bad flags, unreachable export, not root, corrupt index).
.TP
.B 2
Copy completed but some files failed; see
.I failures/
in the work dir. The next
.B sync
retries them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides the
.B \-v
verbosity flag entirely (tracing-subscriber env-filter syntax).
.TP
.B LIBNFS_USE_ALL_RESERVED
Set to 1 by mongoose automatically so libnfs uses the full reserved
port range. Export
.B LIBNFS_USE_ALL_RESERVED=0
to opt out.
.SH FILES
Work-dir layout:
.PP
.nf
<work-dir>/
  run.json                      job identity: source, dest, excludes
  canonical/part-NNNN.parquet   the index
  manifest.json                 run plan
  progress.json                 copy progress + completed-shard list
  failures/part-NNNN.jsonl      per-file failures, per shard
  downgrades/part-NNNN.jsonl    per-file metadata downgrades, per shard
  baseline.json                 which pass the next sync diffs against
  passes/pass-NNNN/             one sync pass (classify results,
                                deleted.jsonl)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
Full copy, then keep it current, then cut over:
.PP
.nf
mongoose copy \\
  --src nfs://old-server/export/data \\
  --dst nfs://new-server/export/data \\
  --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/data \\
  --exclude .snapshot
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/data
# ... stop source writers ...
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/data
mongoose sync --work-dir /var/lib/mongoose/data --cutover
.fi
.PP
Ease off a struggling server (the job resumes at the new level):
.PP
.nf
mongoose copy --src ... --dst ... --work-dir ... --parallel 8
.fi
.SH NOTES
Sync is scan-diff based: each pass is a full metadata rescan diffed
against the previous pass on (file_type, size, mtime, ctime), with
whole-file recopy on any mismatch. Deletions are detected and recorded
but never propagated to the destination. See docs/REFERENCE.md in the
project for the full correctness posture and limitations.
